    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` acceptance test.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**New `Households` helper** (`Households.java`) \u2014 the single source of the deterministic id: first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. Last name is normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case); a missing postcode contributes an empty segment.\n\n**`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 now assigns the householdId *unconditionally* from `Households.id(owner)` (no repository, no `sharesHousehold`, no back-fill). Same last name + postcode \u21d2 same id automatically.\n\n**`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 repurposed into the household duplicate block: rejects a second owner in an existing household (compared by computed `householdId`) with 409, **unless** the request set `sharesHousehold`, which now merely bypasses this block rather than creating the link.\n\n**`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 now keys off the computed `householdId`, and a declared household member (`sharesHousehold` true) is explicitly **not** flagged as a suspected duplicate. Any non-declared owner reaching this step isn't a household duplicate (already 409'd upstream), so it stays unflagged.\n\n**`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 updated the two duplicate steps to consume the `sharesHousehold` variable and refreshed the wiring comments to the new semantics.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 `openapi.yml` (householdId / sharesHousehold / identityKey descriptions + examples) and `DuplicateIdentityException` javadoc updated to describe the (lastName, postcode) household keying.\n\n## One thing worth flagging\nThe spec mentions \"the household-size input to the membership level,\" but `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel` derives the level only from email presence and `namesakeCount` (first+last name) \u2014 there is **no** household-size input in this codebase, so there was nothing there to re-key onto the computed householdId. The duplicate-detection half of that clause is fully implemented. Let me know if you intended a household-size term to be *added* to the membership level.",
